        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in golang.org/x/net/html. This vulnerability allows an attacker to manipulate how HTML is processed and displayed. By providing specially crafted HTML, an attacker can cause an unexpected structure in the rendered output. This can lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks, where malicious scripts are executed in a user's web browser, potentially compromising user data or taking control of their session.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "golang.org/x/net/html: golang: golang.org/x/net/html: Cross-Site Scripting via unexpected HTML tree rendering",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "A flaw in golang.org/x/net/html can lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) in applications that parse and render untrusted HTML, even with sanitization attempts. This is due to an unexpected HTML tree structure, allowing malicious scripts to execute in a user's browser.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
