          {
            "category": "workaround",
            "details": "To mitigate this vulnerability, disable the `proxyproto` plugin in your CoreDNS configuration if it is not strictly required. If the `proxyproto` plugin is essential for your deployment, restrict network access to the CoreDNS service to only trusted sources. This can be achieved by configuring firewall rules to limit UDP traffic on the CoreDNS port. Any changes to the CoreDNS configuration will require a restart or reload of the CoreDNS service to take effect, which may temporarily disrupt DNS resolution.",
